WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.586
The paper makes four contributions.

00:00:03.666 --> 00:00:07.252
First,

00:00:07.332 --> 00:00:10.917
it derives the Tree Neural Tangent Kernel at
initialization for infinitely many perfect

00:00:10.998 --> 00:00:14.583
binary trees of arbitrary depth,

00:00:14.663 --> 00:00:18.249
and proves the kernel stays essentially constant
during training,

00:00:18.329 --> 00:00:21.915
enabling analysis as kernel regression and a proof
of global convergence.

00:00:21.995 --> 00:00:25.581
Second, it shows oblivious ensembles,

00:00:25.661 --> 00:00:29.247
which share splitting rules within each depth as in NODE,

00:00:29.327 --> 00:00:32.913
converge to the very same kernel.

00:00:32.993 --> 00:00:36.578
Third, it characterizes the decision function,

00:00:36.658 --> 00:00:40.244
nearly linear in the basic case and more nonlinear
as splits harden.

00:00:40.324 --> 00:00:43.910
Fourth, it uncovers a degeneracy where deep trees
flatten the kernel.
